  "Number": 4,
  "Question": "For real numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b,\\) define \\(a \\diamond b = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}.\\) What is the value of \\[(5 \\diamond 12) \\diamond ((-12) \\diamond (-5))?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{17}{2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(13\\)",
    "D": "\\(13\\sqrt{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(26\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Evaluate the two inner operations first using the given square-and-add rule. The negative inputs also have positive squares:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n5\\diamond12&=\\sqrt{25+144}=13,\\\\\n(-12)\\diamond(-5)&=\\sqrt{144+25}=13.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nNow apply the same rule to these two outputs:\n\\[\n13\\diamond13=\\sqrt{13^2+13^2}\n=\\sqrt{13^2\\cdot2}=\\boxed{13\\sqrt2}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
